<ansi fg="black-bold">.:</ansi> <ansi fg="magenta">Help for </ansi><ansi fg="command">company meal</ansi>

Feed and water your whole company with one command. Not in a battle: eat
before it starts, or after it ends.

  <ansi fg="command">company eat</ansi>
  Feeds everyone who's hungry.

  <ansi fg="command">company drink</ansi>
  Waters everyone who's thirsty.

  <ansi fg="command">company meal</ansi>
  Both: food first, then drink.

<ansi fg="yellow-bold">Who eats</ansi>

Every living member, you included, the hungriest (or thirstiest) first.
Anyone already Well fed (or Hydrated) is skipped. Each member eats or
drinks one portion per command.

<ansi fg="yellow-bold">What they eat</ansi>

Food and drink come from the company's cargo first, then from the
member's own pack, then from yours. From the first of those with
anything suitable, each member gets the smallest portion that fills
them, or the biggest there is when nothing will. Food that also waters,
like a stew, counts toward thirst, so no one drinks after it who
doesn't need to.

Only plain food and water are used. Anything with another effect, such
as a potion or an ale, is left for you to use by hand with
<ansi fg="command">eat</ansi> or <ansi fg="command">drink</ansi>. Well fed and Hydrated come to you when you eat
food that gives them; companions get the meal itself.

You're told who ate or drank what, where from, and how they feel now,
and who still went without because there was nothing left. The room
sees your company eat.

See also: <ansi fg="command">help survival</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help eat</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help drink</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help cargo</ansi>,
<ansi fg="command">help company inventory</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help company</ansi>.
